' What the automated pass cannot see.
'
' The generator reads data members and nothing else. A facet of free functions
' has no class to hang off, a type declared inside another type has no box of
' its own, and static and using members are skipped. The notes below fill those
' in. Each names its class fully qualified rather than reopening a namespace,
' because this PlantUML version crashes when a namespace that already holds
' classes is declared a second time. Redeclaring a class merges the members
' below into the box the automated pass drew, so a refresh keeps both.

note as OresMarketdataDatumHelpers
    Free functions in ores::marketdata::datum:
    ore_name(instrument_type t) : string_view
    ore_name(quote_type t) : string_view
    instrument_type_named(name) : optional<instrument_type>
    quote_type_named(name) : optional<quote_type>
    name_of(field f) : string_view
    field_named(name) : optional<field>
    codes_of(field f) : span<const string_view>
    name_of(asset_class a) : string_view
    asset_class_named(name) : optional<asset_class>
    name_of(index_family f) : string_view
    index_family_named(name) : optional<index_family>
    kind_of(field f) : value_kind
    schema_of(instrument_type t) : const schema_row&
    index_row_of(index_family f) : const index_row&
    series_of(d) : market_datum
    datum_at(series, coordinates) : expected<market_datum, string>
    datum_at_point(series, point) : expected<market_datum, string>
    parse_value(field f, text) : expected<value, string>
    text_of(const value& v) : string
    The enums and the text a key carries meet here and nowhere else.
    A name_of / *_named pair reads one enum both ways; codes_of gives
    a code field's accepted tokens; kind_of gives a field's value
    type. schema_of and index_row_of index the two tables by the
    enum's own value, so each table's order is its enum's order.
    series_of keeps a datum's identity fields; datum_at and
    datum_at_point put coordinates back. text_of writes a value as
    the key spells it, or the empty string for none.

    Free functions in ores::marketdata::datum::detail:
    id(f), id_or_none(f), at(f), at_or_none(f) : field_spec
    rows_follow_the_enum(), no_row_repeats_a_field(),
    every_row_has_an_identity(), every_subject_always_names_the_series(),
    index_rows_follow_the_enum() : bool
    The four id/at forms mark a field as identity or coordinate and
    say whether the key may leave it out. The predicates are
    constexpr and run in static_asserts: a schema row out of enum
    order, a repeated field, a row with no identity, or a subject
    that can be none fails the build.
end note

