note as OresMarketdataDomainHelpers
    Free functions in ores::marketdata::domain:
    asset_class_for_authority(authority) : optional<string_view>
    feed_conflict_key(qualifier, role) : string
    synthetic_tick_wildcard() : string
    market_tick_wildcard() : string
    synthetic_tick_subject(source_name) : string
    market_tick_subject(tenant_id, workspace_id, party_id, ore_key) : string
    asset_class_for_authority maps an oresmd authority to the refdata
    asset class the catalogue declares; an authority that maps to
    none, such as a pairwise correlation or the generic wrapper,
    answers nullopt. feed_conflict_key joins a feed's qualifier and
    role with a unit separator, so two feeds conflict when the key is
    equal: a discount curve and a projection curve for one qualifier
    coexist, and a feed with no role still has a deterministic key.
    synthetic_tick_subject builds synthetic.v1.ops.tick.<source>.
    market_tick_subject extends market_tick's subject with the
    consumer and the datum's canonical ORE key, lower-cased with its
    slashes turned to dots. The two wildcards subscribe to every
    producer's or every consumer's ticks.
end note

