class ores::marketdata::messaging::list_market_series_request <<struct>> {
    {static} +nats_subject : string_view
}
note right of "ores::marketdata::messaging::list_market_series_request"
Every one of the 71 request structs carries a using response_type
alias naming its reply and a static nats_subject, both declared
inside the request; the automated pass skips using and static lines,
so neither reaches the box and the alias has no box of its own.
Subjects read marketdata.v1.<resource>.<verb>, and a version family
adds _versions. Each request also carries static requires_session,
true wherever a call must establish a session first. The market_tick
payload carries nats_subject and requires_session = false, and no
response_type, because nothing replies to it.
end note

